	(text "Per fig 18 of the DRV5023 Datasheet\nStandard Circuit"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.548 71.628 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "09384355-0f70-4d67-8ee1-119a8ca9e896")
	)
	(text "The DRV5023 output stage uses an open-drain NMOS, and it is rated to sink up to 30 mA of current. For proper\noperation, calculate the value of the pullup resistor R1 using :\nVref max / 30mA <= R1 <= Vref min / 100μA\nThe size of R1 is a tradeoff between the OUT rise time and the current when OUT is pulled low. A lower current\nis generally better, however faster transitions and bandwidth require a smaller resistor for faster switching.\nIn addition, ensure that the value of R1 > 500 Ω to ensure the output driver can pull the OUT pin close to GND.\n - Datasheet p.14\n\nFor our 5V circuit:\n5.25V / 30mA <= R1 <= 4.75V / 100μA\n5.25V / 0.03A <= R1 <= 4.75V / 0.0001 A\n175 <= R1 <= 47500\n10kΩ well within range of min 175Ω to 47.5kΩ"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.052 33.528 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "682610df-0c79-4b11-80d5-bc118e4a7cc0")
	)
	(text "Pullup 10k\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 129.54 39.116 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6c2bad38-9b68-40ca-a042-de3ed24d9533")
	)
	(text "2.5 to 38 V power supply. Bypass this pin to the GND pin with a 0.01-μF (minimum)\nceramic capacitor rated for VCC - Datasheet p.4\n\nConsidering our power supply distance is relatively high (about 50cm of wires) \nand there are many stack connectors, there is increased inductance, so we chose\na higher capacitor of 100nF instead of 10nF / 0,01μF"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.052 57.404 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8174bab2-b154-4e4c-9704-cd930d93bb21")
	)
	(text "Pull Up Resistor"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 169.926 20.574 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "aa92fbd4-5984-4c33-ad41-e211b25d4304")
	)
